---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — EUROPA"
  description="EUROPA email subscriptions, hosting and browser preferences."
  bodyClass="privacy-page"
>
  <SiteHeader section="privacy" />
  <main id="main-content" class="privacy-main">
    <header class="privacy-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">EUROPA</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <div>
        <p>
          If you subscribe, Bård Standal and Brevo use your email address to
          manage the subscription and send the updates you requested.
        </p>
        <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated 23 July 2026</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content">
      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-controller">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-controller">Who is responsible</h2>
          <p>
            Bård Standal is responsible for the personal information described on
            this page. For questions, requests or privacy concerns, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:bard.standal@gmail.com">bard.standal@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-subscription">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-subscription">Email updates</h2>
          <p>
            If you subscribe, your email address is used to manage the
            subscription and send updates about EUROPA and new work on European
            history.
          </p>
          <p>
            The legal basis is your consent. When you submit the form, the address
            is added to EUROPA’s update list. The subscription record includes the
            time, source and recorded consent field.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can withdraw consent at any time through the unsubscribe link in
            every notification or by emailing the address above. Withdrawing consent
            does not affect the lawful use of your details before withdrawal.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-retention">Email-list retention</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Active subscriber details are kept until you unsubscribe or ask for
              deletion.
            </li>
            <li>
              After an unsubscribe request, a minimal suppression record may be kept
              for as long as needed to honour that choice and prevent accidental
              re-subscription. It is not used to send messages.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-services">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-services">Services that process information</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Brevo</strong> processes subscriber details, subscription,
            delivery and unsubscribe records as a data processor for EUROPA.
            Brevo processes this information on Bård Standal’s documented
            instructions under a data processing agreement. You can read{" "}
            <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
              Brevo’s privacy information
            </a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            EUROPA does not ask subscribers for separate email-pixel tracking
            consent. Brevo is therefore configured not to attach recipient-level
            open or click tracking to contacts whose tracking consent is unknown.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts and delivers the public site. Like
            any hosting service, it necessarily receives connection and request
            metadata to deliver and secure the pages. EUROPA does not receive
            GitHub Pages’ raw server logs. This necessary processing is based on
            the legitimate interest in operating a secure public website. See the{" "}
            <a
              href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              GitHub General Privacy Statement
            </a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            These providers publish information about their subprocessors and
            international-transfer arrangements. Their current notices and the
            applicable data processing agreements govern those arrangements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-storage">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">05</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-storage">Browser preferences</h2>
          <p>
            If you dismiss the email invitation, EUROPA stores a first-party
            functional preference in your browser’s local storage for seven days.
            It records only that the invitation was dismissed, so that it does
            not interrupt you again during that period. It is not used to identify
            you, measure your reading or share information with another service.
          </p>
          <p>
            After a successful signup, a second functional preference records that
            the invitation should not be shown again. It remains until you clear the
            site’s browser data. Neither preference contains a name, email address or
            Brevo identifier.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can remove the preference at any time by clearing site data in your
            browser. The invitation will then be eligible to appear again.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
        <p class="privacy-section__number" aria-hidden="true">06</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-rights">Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You may ask for access to the personal information held about you, have
            inaccurate information corrected, request deletion or restriction, and
            receive the information you supplied in a portable format where
            applicable. You may also withdraw consent at any time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Start by contacting{" "}
            <a href="mailto:bard.standal@gmail.com">bard.standal@gmail.com</a>.
            You also have the right to{" "}
            <a
              href="https://www.datatilsynet.no/en/about-us/contact-us/how-to-complain-to-the-norwegian-dpa/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              complain to the Norwegian Data Protection Authority
            </a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
